Theory Details-

1) To get the details faster for any type of search, we have used elastic search.
2) Elastic search always used as a secondary DB as we can't do joins and all like we do in sql.
Elastic search always gets updated via CDC pipeline. We would need to handle consistency if we try to update
 in 2 db(sql, elastic search).
3) For booking we are having 2 steps -
    (1) we reserve the booking, reserve can only wait for a certain time ex: 5min
    (2) complete the booking
4) At a time multiple can try to update the booking, In this case putting locks on db and use a cron job
to remove reserved entries if user has not booked in the 5min window. In this if cron job didn't run for 1 cycle
then the seat will be reserved for longer amount of time.
5) There is a better way to handle case (point - 4 ). We can use radis to keep all the reserved seat entries
 for TTL -5min.In this way it we can handle deletion of revered seats and also won't cause load on DB.
6) Now during peak Event, as our system can take only x load and have y seats available. but traffic is 100x.
In this case we need to use virtual waiting queue. So after a certain limit, users request waits in the virtual queue and
once the current load decreases, requests which are in waiting queue would be pulled.
7) this Queue can be a redis/DB, in which data can be stored in sorted set / list. Here we use redis sortedset so that
if user wants to fetch the status of the request, it can be fetched in logn time, meaning how many users are ahead of him.
8) how to handle redis failures for reserved seats - In this case, an another instance can take place, but we
 loose all the reserved requests. At this time if some other user comes and try to book, they will be able to book.
 In this user experience will hamper but consistency will be maintained


